    <statement><p>Suppose <m>y = -2 \cos{ (4 t + 11 )} - 4</m>. In your answers, enter <em>pi</em> for <m>\pi</m>.</p>
<p>What is the horizontal shift? <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{-11}{4}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>



 To find the horizontal shift, we factor out a 4 within the cosine function, giving us
<me>y = -2 \cos{ (4 t + 11 )} - 4 = -2 \cos{ \big( 4 (t + \frac{11}{4}) \big) } - 4</me>
Thus, the horizontal shift is  <m>-\frac{11}{4}</m>.



</solution>
